From d7e08aecfa4b4462a14cb6ea52d40febad625944 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:09:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] apk: record provided names and resolve source-package aliases
 when matching

Some apk-based distributions publish advisories under a name that is not
the apk origin of the installed package: BellSoft keys the Liberica JDK
advisories on "openjdk<major>[-lite]" while the origin is
"liberica<major>[-lite]"; the binary package carries the alias in its
provides list:

    P:liberica21-lite-jdk-no-deps  o:liberica21-lite
    p:java-jdk-no-deps java21-jdk-no-deps openjdk21-lite-jdk-no-deps=21.0.2_p14-r1

osv.dev does not resolve the alias (34 records for openjdk21-lite /
Alpaquita:23, none for liberica21-lite), so the matchers have to.

* apk extractor: the plain package names of the "p:" field are kept in
  Metadata.Provides (so:/cmd:/pc:/path entries dropped).
* osvutil.QueryNames: candidate names in preference order - origin, every
  provided name, every provided name with the sub-package suffix stripped
  ("-jdk-no-deps") - for the Alpaquita and BellSoft Hardened Containers
  ecosystems only; every other ecosystem keeps a single name.
* vulnmatch/osvdev and vulnmatch/osvlocal try the candidates in order; the
  first name the source knows wins.
